# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

.DS_Store

# Secrets / env — never commit real credentials (BR6, INV-02)
.env*
!.env.example
# HARDEN M5 (2026-09-23): the rule was `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`,
# which left `.env.bak`, `.env.backup`, `.env.production` and friends
# COMMITTABLE -- verified with `git check-ignore`. On a publicly readable
# repo one `cp .env .env.bak` is a credential disclosure. `.env*` + an
# explicit un-ignore for the template closes the family.

# Editor swap / backup files (QA-S-01.3 hygiene)
*.swp
*.swo
.*.sw[a-p]
*~

# Local per-run artifact (ADR-0007 Option E, 2026-09-23) -- carries the
# full CT-02 verdict map (expected/actual/confidence/verdict); the
# platform stays value-free (DEBT-18 option B unchanged). Never commit.
.idp-regression-run-artifacts/

# Golden-set seed data (CLAUDE.md ## Domain: treat golden-set contents as
# sensitive). The golden's authoritative home is its Langfuse dataset
# items, not a copy in git history -- and this repo is publicly readable.
# The files stay on disk where the CLI and scripts expect them
# (scripts/provision_golden_dataset.py reads id_seeds/golden_set.json);
# they are simply never committed. Today's three seeds are synthetic, but
# the rule exists so a golden derived from a real customer document can
# never land here by habit. See id_seeds/README.md.
id_seeds/

# Scheduled-run artifacts (scripts/run_eval_scheduled.sh + the launchd
# template) -- per-run dated logs and failure markers, none of which are
# source. Matched by extension, not by ignoring the `logs/` directory
# itself, so the `.gitkeep` files that keep it present for a fresh
# clone stay tracked.
logs/
!logs/**/.gitkeep

# The overlap-prevention lock file scripts/run_eval_scheduled.sh creates
# next to the repo root (an empty file `lockf` holds an advisory lock
# on -- never real content, never to be committed).
.idp-regression-scheduled-run.lock

# Batch operator-tool output (2026-09-24): the noise-floor report
# (scripts/noise_floor.py) and the draft golden sets + raw captures
# scripts/bootstrap_golden_set.py writes. Same rule as the run artifact
# and id_seeds/ above -- these carry extracted values from real customer
# documents, and this repo is publicly readable. Written owner-only by
# the tools; ignored here so a stray --out path cannot be committed by
# habit.
.idp-regression-noise-floor/
*.captures/
*draft_golden_set*.json

# Per-file pin store (scripts/pin_document.py, verify_document.py,
# compare_versions.py) and the corpus pipeline's work dir
# (scripts/golden_pipeline.py). Both hold the THREE most sensitive things
# these tools touch: the customer documents themselves (unpacked from the
# operator's zip), the raw IDP responses, and the goldens -- the same
# extracted financial values `## Domain` calls out. Written owner-only by
# the tools; ignored here because this repo is publicly readable and one
# `git add -A` would otherwise commit a customer's invoices.
# (Filed 2026-09-25: these two were COMMITTABLE for a day -- `git
# check-ignore` said so -- while `.idp-regression-run-artifacts/` and
# `.idp-regression-noise-floor/` were already covered.)
.idp-regression-pins/
.idp-regression-pipeline/

# ── Sweep 2026-09-25: every generated path the tools write ────────────
# Verified with `git check-ignore` against each default, and verified
# with `git ls-files` that none of these patterns matches a file that is
# already TRACKED on purpose (`testpack/golden_set.json`,
# `tests/fixtures/live/*.raw.json` -- both synthetic, both deliberate).

# Raw IDP responses, wherever a tool is pointed. A capture is the
# extractor's verbatim answer for a real document: field values,
# confidences, the lot. The two committed ones live under
# `tests/fixtures/live/` and were curated for that purpose (SR-1); a
# working `captures/` directory is never that.
captures/

# Golden sets and everything derived from them, at ANY --out path.
# `## Domain`: a golden's authoritative home is its dataset item on the
# platform, not a copy in this (publicly readable) repo -- the same rule
# `id_seeds/` above is ignored under.
*.golden.json
*.pins.json
*.calibrated.json
*.calibration.json
*.calibration.md
*.review.md
noise-floor-*.json

# Coverage output (measured ad hoc; no coverage dependency is installed,
# but a `--cov` run or a stdlib `trace` dump should never land in a commit).
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.cover

# Editor / IDE / OS scratch not already covered above.
.idea/
.vscode/
Thumbs.db


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Epic E — the local console (src/idp_regression/ui/ + frontend/).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uploaded archives and the documents unpacked from them. These are the
# CUSTOMER'S FILES, not just values extracted from them — the one thing
# `## Domain` says never leaves the machine. Owner-only on disk; ignored
# here so a `git add -A` after a demo cannot commit an invoice.
.idp-regression-uploads/

# The built frontend and its dependencies. `dist/` is generated by
# `npm run build` and served by the console; neither belongs in a commit.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: `.idp-regression-scorers/`. A scorer spec
# holds rules, never extracted values, and it configures the GATE —
# committing it is what makes a custom gate reviewable. See
# `src/idp_regression/ui/custom_scorers.py`.

# Job state for the local console (Epic E, tickets 6-7).
# `.idp-regression-jobs/` holds one record per job — command, approved
# extraction count, verdict — and deliberately NOT the job's output,
# which carries extracted values and already lives in the gitignored run
# artifact. It is still per-machine runtime state rather than config, so
# it is not committed. `.lock` is the flock that admits one
# quota-spending job per workspace.
.idp-regression-jobs/
.idp-regression-jobs.lock
